    {
      "index": 38,
      "tag": "div",
      "attrs": {
        "class": "flex-vertical whitney theme-dark"
      },
      "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDiscord\nThe Chaos Elemental's basic attack, made up of green particles that deal either   or  damage to the player. His other attacks are variations of this move with different effects.\nMadness\n⬥ The Chaos Elemental launches a multicoloured attack. Upon hit, the player's main hand weapon and up to 3 other pieces of equipped gear will be unequipped and placed in their inventory.\n    • If the player's inventory is full, the Chaos Elemental will not use this attack\n    • Click to view an example of Madness.\nConfusion\n⬥ The Chaos Elemental launches an attack made of fire. Upon hit, the player will be teleported upwards of 20 tiles away from Chaos Elemental in a random direction.\n    • The player will stop attacking the boss after being teleported, be sure to click on the Chaos Elemental once this happens to resume attacking.\n    • Click to view an example of Confusion\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 166188,
        "end": 168670
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 168670,
        "end": 168672
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "tag": "p",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "​",
      "location": {
        "start": 168672,
        "end": 168687
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 168687,
        "end": 168688
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "tag": "h2",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "tips-and-tricks"
      },
      "text": "Tips and Tricks",
      "location": {
        "start": 168688,
        "end": 168744
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 168744,
        "end": 168745
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "tag": "p",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "⬥ The  hit of Discord is the most accurate, making it best to either Protect from Magic  or Soul Split  throughout the fight.",
      "location": {
        "start": 168745,
        "end": 169250
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 169250,
        "end": 169251
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "tag": "p",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "⬥ Prioritize using powerful threshold abilities, only using basic abilities to build up to stronger ones, or when better options are on cooldown.",
      "location": {
        "start": 169251,
        "end": 169403
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 169403,
        "end": 169404
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "tag": "p",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• For Ranged  examples of powerful abilities are Snap Shot  and Rapid Fire , with abilities like Dazing Shot  and Piercing Shot  being your weaker basics. Death's Swiftness  is a very powerful ability, but should only be used near the start of the fight, if you find yourself with too much adrenaline.",
      "location": {
        "start": 169404,
        "end": 170430
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 170430,
        "end": 170431
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "tag": "p",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• For Necromancy  build up to abilities like Volley of Souls  and Finger of Death  with your weaker abilities, Soul Sap  and Touch of Death , using your Basic Attack  when all else is on cooldown.",
      "location": {
        "start": 170431,
        "end": 171401
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 171401,
        "end": 171402
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "tag": "p",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "⬥ If possible, keep your inventory full of items to avoid the Madness special attack, Chaos Elemental's drops can be used to fill any blank spaces.",
      "location": {
        "start": 171402,
        "end": 171556
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 171556,
        "end": 171557
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "tag": "p",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "⬥ An NPC named Edward, located outside the Dragonkin Laboratory, south-east of the level 50 Wilderness Obelisk, can be used as a bank to store any drops the player receives and resupply for longer trips.",
      "location": {
        "start": 171557,
        "end": 171767
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 171767,
        "end": 171768
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "tag": "p",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "⬥ Due to the Chaos Elemental being located in the Wilderness, all Wilderness based bonuses granted by the Infernal Puzzle Box  work against this boss.",
      "location": {
        "start": 171768,
        "end": 172063
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "tag": "#text",
      "attrs": {},
      "text": "\n",
      "location": {
        "start": 172063,
        "end": 172064
      }
    },
